# ==============================================================================
# Third-party press text — NOT redistributable
#
# The published dataset card (data/hf_dataset/README.md) states the policy:
#   "Press rows have raw_text stripped (all 3,425). Those are third-party news
#    articles and are not redistributed here in any form."
# CC BY 4.0 covers only the annotation layer (mechanism, direction, polarity,
# dates, derived columns) — not the source passages.
#
# The paths below hold the UNSTRIPPED text and would contradict that policy:
#   data/raw/*/press/   769 full GDELT news articles (.txt)
#   data/processed/     ptc_pool*.jsonl — 3,449 press rows with raw_text
#
# They also carry third-party PII: 47 unique work email addresses of named
# journalists (WSJ, Thomson Reuters) and corporate staff (Sanofi), scraped
# into the article text. Most are EU data subjects.
#
# NOTE: app/demo/*_ptc_pool.jsonl is deliberately NOT ignored. Those pools have
# had press raw_text stripped (3,449 rows nulled, spans cleared) and keep only
# management raw_text, so they match the published policy and the demo app
# still works from a clean clone. Regenerate with:
#     python scripts/build_demo_bundle.py <TICKER>
# and re-strip press raw_text before committing the result.
# ==============================================================================
data/raw/
data/processed/

# ==============================================================================
# Large derived artefacts — regenerable, too big to publish
#   data/interim/   147 MB of Titan embeddings (.npy) + indices
#   data/market/    yfinance price/earnings cache. Yahoo's terms restrict
#                   redistribution of their market data; it is also trivially
#                   re-fetchable, so it does not belong in the repo.
# ==============================================================================
data/interim/
data/market/

# The "documents" config is 80 M characters of management source text and the
# embeddings config is model-specific and large. Both are served from the
# Hugging Face dataset instead: tomPrdd/ptc-pool-eu-largecap
data/hf_dataset/documents/
data/hf_dataset/embeddings/

# ==============================================================================
