#   article/  UNPUBLISHED drafts for tompradaude.com, with placeholder
#             APP_URL / REPO_URL links still unfilled
#   new_doc/  scratch staging directory
# ==============================================================================
doc/
article/
new_doc/

# ==============================================================================
# Internal operations documentation
#
# docs/CLEANUP_PLAN.md documents the S3 bucket prefix layout, object counts,
# storage costs, retention decisions, and records a past incident in which the
# bucket served 492 verbatim news articles world-readable. Useful internally,
# but it maps private infrastructure and advertises a resolved exposure.
# ==============================================================================
docs/CLEANUP_PLAN.md

# ==============================================================================
# NESTED GIT REPOSITORY — ACTION REQUIRED BEFORE THE FIRST COMMIT
#
# packages/ptc-extract contains its own .git (github.com/tomPrdd/ptc-extract)
# but is NOT registered as a submodule. `git add` records it as a bare gitlink
# (mode 160000), so GitHub shows an empty, unclickable folder.
#
# It is deliberately NOT ignored here: pyproject.toml declares it as a uv
# workspace member and a hard dependency —
#     dependencies = ["ptc-extract[bedrock]"]
#     [tool.uv.workspace] members = ["packages/*"]
#     [tool.uv.sources]   ptc-extract = { workspace = true }
#     pythonpath = ["src", "packages/ptc-extract/src"]
# so excluding it would break `uv sync`, `import ptc_extraction` and pytest
# for anyone who clones the repo.
#
# Resolve it one of these ways before committing:
#   1. Vendor it as normal files:  rm -rf packages/ptc-extract/.git
#   2. Make it a real submodule:   git submodule add \
#        https://github.com/tomPrdd/ptc-extract packages/ptc-extract
# Its own build cruft is ignored either way:
packages/ptc-extract/.DS_Store
packages/ptc-extract/dist/
packages/ptc-extract/.venv/

